// `==` over a POLYMORPHIC sum, proven to the bottom. This fixture was born RED
// on 2026-09-18 and turned green the same day by proof, which is the whole
// life of an expected-red entry and worth keeping visible.
//
// WHAT IT CAUGHT: two structurally equal `Some(BInt(7))` answered UNEQUAL, and
// the emitted helper said why — `$eq_nOption`, ONE helper for every
// instantiation, loading `Some`'s payload at offset 4 and comparing it with
// `(i32.eq)`. Two reads dropped a proof the graph held. `fold_sig` rendered
// `TName(n, args)` as the bare name, where `TList` / `TTuple` / `TRecord` all
// fold their payloads, so `Option(Boxed)` and `Option(Int)` shared one helper
// that could not know which it served; and `variant_specs_of` answered with
// the constructor's DECLARED payload type — the quantified var — which
// `emit_field_eq`'s last arm turned into a word compare with no diagnostic.
//
// It was invisible to `T_EqTypeUnprovable`, whose whole census held unchanged
// across the discovery: that diagnostic reports at an AUTHORED comparison
// whose operand type is a variable, and here the authored operands are proven
// `Option(Boxed)` on both sides. The unprovable operand lives inside a
// GENERATED leaf, where no authored span points.
//
// The control is the point of the shape: the monomorphic `BInt(7) == BInt(7)`
// was RIGHT on the same run, because there every declared payload is ground.
// So the exit NAMES which halves are broken rather than merely failing —
// measured 6 before the fix (wrapped int 2 + wrapped text 4), 0 after.
// expect: 0

type Boxed = BInt(Int) | BText(String)

fn main() = {
  let control = if BInt(7) == BInt(7) { 0 } else { 1 }
  let wrapped = if Some(BInt(7)) == Some(BInt(7)) { 0 } else { 2 }
  let text = if Some(BText("ab")) == Some(BText(str_concat("a", "b"))) { 0 } else { 4 }
  control + wrapped + text
}
